KG42.register("edges-d9b02fdef82032e33fabf23b",{"id":"S-9585d7df56ee7f60","source":"COMP-72f84a438787fbd5","type":"precedes","target":"COMP-c98744ae891e04fd","evidence_class":"S","scientific_acceptance":false,"relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"paper_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction"],"assertions":[{"id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E003","paper":"20-storage_sharing_auction","rule_id":"v141-c-R001","rule_ref":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E003","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"clearing.local","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-72f84a438787fbd5","target":"COMP-c98744ae891e04fd","source_occurrence_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::V::matching.counterparties","target_occurrence_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::V::clearing.local","source_unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::matching.counterparties","target_unit_id":"20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-a-M01::clearing.local","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. | Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. | Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. | Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. | The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. | The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. | The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"ffd50cb5717e76f5f90ded989682aa2432a895d7d2b5af44f1578b1a10711688","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","source_definition":"The auctioneer determines the preliminary participating SFC and RU groups through cutoff counts K and J obtained from the intersection of the aggregate supply and demand curves. Scope: Community joint energy-storage ownership auction; determination of preliminary participant cutoffs before marginal-participant exclusion. Condition: The supply–demand intersection cutoffs satisfy a_K ≥ r_J. RUs outside {1, 2, ..., J} and SFCs outside {1, 2, ..., K} are removed from the auction process. Scope: Community joint energy-storage ownership auction; exclusion of parties beyond the intersection cutoffs. Condition: After K and J are determined, a_m \u003c r_i for every SFC outside {1, 2, ..., K} and RU outside {1, 2, ..., J}. The joint storage-sharing group is restricted to K − 1 SFCs and J − 1 RUs, excluding the marginal SFC K and RU J. Scope: Community joint energy-storage ownership auction; participant-group restriction for a truthful auction. Condition: J and K have been determined and auction truthfulness is required. SFC K and RU J may also participate in the joint storage-sharing trading group. Scope: Community joint energy-storage ownership auction; optional inclusion of marginal participants. Condition: A truthful auction is not a necessity.","target_definition":"The auctioneer performs local allocation by allocating ES spaces for sharing to each SFC according to the auction's allocation rule. Scope: Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. Determination of the participating RU and SFC trading groups precedes execution of the storage allocation rule. Scope: The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. Matching total ES demand and supply while maintaining a truthful auction requires selecting J −1 RUs and K −1 SFCs for joint sharing. Scope: Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. Condition: A truthful auction is required, and the determination rule has established J and K. Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its entire equilibrium offered amount. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs is less than or equal to total ES requested by the participating SFCs. Each RU's allocated ES contribution equals its equilibrium offered amount minus its assigned oversupply burden, truncated at zero. Scope: Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total equilibrium ES offered by the participating RUs exceeds total ES requested by the participating SFCs. Each participating RU bears an equal oversupply burden, calculated as total excess ES divided by J −1. Scope: Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES. Each RU is assigned an oversupply burden proportional to its reservation price. Scope: The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the reservation-price-proportional alternative is used. Replacing the reservation price with the equilibrium offered ES amount in rule (17) assigns each RU an oversupply burden proportional to its shared ES amount. Scope: The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. Condition: Total offered ES exceeds total requested ES, and the ES-quantity-proportional variant is used.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Determination of the participating RU and SFC trading groups precedes execution of the storage allocation rule. Scope: The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties","clearing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E26"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-A. Determination Rule","anchor_text":"no on Fig. 3. Determination of the Vickrey price, the maximum auction price, and To the number of pa","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"The proposed scheme initially determines the set of SFCs $\\subset \\mathcal{M}$ and RUs $\\subset \\mathcal{N}$ that will effectively take part in the auction mechanism once the upper bound of the auction price $p_t^{\\max}$ is determined. Eventually, the payment and the allocation rules are executed in the course of the auction plan."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-441686b1ee-p08-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV-F. Adaptation to Time-Varying Case","anchor_text":"ual fashion where each time slot has a suitable time duration based on the type of application, e.g.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To this end, first we note that once the number of participating RUs and SFCs is decided for a particular time slot via the determination rule, the rest of the procedures, i.e., the payment and allocation rules are executed following the descriptions in Section IV-B and IV-D respectively for the respective time slot. Now, if the total number of RUs and SFCs is fixed, the RUs and SFCs that participate in the modified auction scheme in any time slot is determined by their respective reservation and bidding prices for that time slot."}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Allocation rule (16) for the participating J−1 RUs and K−1 SFCs in the community ES-sharing auction. | Equal allocation rule (18), adopted for the remainder of the paper's community ES-sharing analysis. | Matching total ES demand and supply in the truthful branch of the community auction. | Storage allocation within the community's modified ES-sharing auction. | The ES-quantity-proportional variant of allocation rule (17) considered for the community ES-sharing auction. | The community ES-sharing auction and its execution within each time slot of the time-varying extension. | The reservation-price-proportional allocation alternative considered for the community ES-sharing auction.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E22","v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E07","v141-b-g02-E20","v141-b-g02-E21","v141-b-g02-E22","v141-b-g02-E23","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R001-E003","source":"matching.counterparties","target":"clearing.local","type":"precedes","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E26","v141-b-g02-E26"]},"paper_scope_note":"Initial selection boundary, removal of marginal participants, Stackelberg price, and spatial response are kept separate; this is limited to component use in this auction protocol and does not prove a unique equilibrium or real-world operation."}}],"assertion_ids":["20-storage_sharing_auction::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E003"]});
